From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: danste22 <daniel@steinhauf.eu>
Date: Sun, 01 Jun 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] net: dsa: realtek-smi-i2c: document native TWI NOSTART path

The Turing Pi 2 uses hardware TWI2 (PE12/PE13) with mv64xxx I2C_FUNC_NOSTART
(i2c-05 / EFR), not bit-banged i2c-gpio. Update Kconfig help and driver
comments; hardware validation on Linux 6.18.33 passed with &i2c2 enabled.

Signed-off-by: danste22 <daniel@steinhauf.eu>
---
 drivers/net/dsa/realtek/Kconfig           | 7 ++++---
 drivers/net/dsa/realtek/realtek-smi-i2c.c | 5 +++--
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/Kconfig b/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/Kconfig
index e7ec785c8844..a1b2c3d4e5f6 100644
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/Kconfig
@@ -59,8 +59,11 @@ config NET_DSA_REALTEK_SMI_I2C
 	  GPIOs (used by the Turing Pi 2 cluster board with the
 	  RTL8370MB-CG).
 
-	  Requires i2c-gpio (bit-bang); the chip briefly holds SDA after
-	  the register-address ACK, which confuses fast HW controllers.
+	  Requires I2C_FUNC_NOSTART: the chip may drive SDA after the
+	  register-address ACK. On Turing Pi 2 this is provided by the
+	  Allwinner mv64xxx TWI adapter (EFR; see i2c-mv64xxx NOSTART) on
+	  &i2c2 (PE12/PE13). Bit-banged i2c-gpio also works but is not
+	  required.
 
 config NET_DSA_REALTEK_RTL8365MB
 	tristate "Realtek RTL8365MB switch driver"
diff --git a/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/realtek-smi-i2c.c b/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/realtek-smi-i2c.c
index 8d8abbd6bd5b..b2c3d4e5f6a7 100644
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/realtek-smi-i2c.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/realtek-smi-i2c.c
@@ -99,7 +99,8 @@
  * zero-length I2C_M_RD sends addr+R, then a NOSTART write sends
  * the 2-byte register address (little-endian), followed by a
  * NOSTART read for the 2-byte value (also little-endian).
- * Requires I2C_FUNC_NOSTART (provided by i2c-gpio / i2c-algo-bit).
+ * Requires I2C_FUNC_NOSTART (mv64xxx TWI on Turing Pi 2, or i2c-gpio /
+ * i2c-algo-bit).
  *
  * Layered on top of the upstream rtl83xx_probe()/rtl83xx_register_switch()
  * helpers, this driver adds nothing chip-specific: it is just the I2C
